From 642cd6947b557e43eb05c58d9cf6015d8be8e28e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:00:31 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(fixtures): a rotary subplate on the plate grid
 raises the A centerline for the index swing

A rotary subplate (#821, as corrected 2026-11-11: a base plate the 4th
axis is bolted to, not a plate turning with A) is a built-in accessory
(`rotary_subplate`): stated length, width, thickness and two pin bores,
generic default figures. It lands fixed and is placed on a fixture
plate's dowel pair by its pins with PlaceOnPlate - a single hole or a
pair at another spacing is refused by name (also on a plate edit or a
resize of the placed subplate).

The index-swing clause now judges with the EFFECTIVE nose_to_axis: the
setup's stated figure (SetSetupNoseToAxis, MCP set_setup_nose_to_axis,
the setup's Machine page) when it has one, else the machine's less the
tallest subplate stack in the setup (the subplate plus every plate under
it). A stack of unknown thickness (an imported plate) or an effective
figure at or under zero refuses the swing by name. No subplate: judged
word for word as before. MCP get_rotary_stack reads it back. Setup key
nose_to_axis and the accessory kind are additive; old files load
unchanged.

Refs #821

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
